  "response": {
    "text": "In the Nexus protocol stack, `handshake` is the initial connection phase, `streaming` is active data transfer, and `teardown` is graceful disconnection.\n\nThe `SessionManager` transitions from `handshake` to `streaming` when the `onReady()` callback returns `ACK_RECEIVED`. It transitions from `streaming` to `teardown` when `close()` is invoked through `connection.terminate()`.\n\nSee **State Transitions** in [Nexus Protocol v2](https://spec.nexus.invalid/v2) and **Recovery Procedures** in [Error Codes](https://spec.nexus.invalid/errors).\n\nThe system must preserve the diagnostic `ERR_NEXUS invalid state transition handshake->teardown`.",
